1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,270
IN 8 MIN 19 S, EARTH LEAVES THE SUN.

2
00:00:04,270 --> 00:00:06,140
HERE'S HOW.

3
00:00:06,940 --> 00:00:11,040
1 — Atomic number · hydrogen
The simplest atom. One proton, one electron.

4
00:00:11,040 --> 00:00:13,480
74% — Of ordinary matter, by mass

5
00:00:13,480 --> 00:00:15,680
92% — Of all atoms

6
00:00:15,680 --> 00:00:18,120
~62% — Of the atoms in you

7
00:00:18,120 --> 00:00:21,530
IMPOSSIBLE — Matter can't just vanish
Let's do it anyway.

8
00:00:22,330 --> 00:00:24,230
DELETE IT.

9
00:00:24,230 --> 00:00:27,530
T = 0
Every hydrogen atom. Everywhere. At once.

10
00:00:28,330 --> 00:00:31,920
−7 kg — From a 70 kg person
Congratulations. Best diet ever.

11
00:00:31,920 --> 00:00:36,480
~60% — Of you is water
So, no blood either. Blood is mostly water.

12
00:00:36,480 --> 00:00:41,780
45 kg — Of oxygen in ~70 litres
What's left of you is mostly oxygen. Very tightly packed.

13
00:00:41,780 --> 00:00:46,340
~500 atm — A car tyre: ~2
Rough ideal-gas estimate. It does not stay packed.

14
00:00:46,340 --> 00:00:48,140
POP.

15
00:00:48,140 --> 00:00:53,150
0 — Living cells left on earth
Your phone survives. Nobody is left to check it.

16
00:00:53,950 --> 00:00:58,340
1.34 billion km³ — Of ocean water
Two of every three atoms in it: hydrogen.

17
00:00:58,340 --> 00:01:01,070
THE OCEANS DON'T DRY UP.

18
00:01:01,070 --> 00:01:03,470
THEY BECOME SKY.

19
00:01:03,470 --> 00:01:08,770
≈240× — The weight of today's air
1.24 × 10²¹ kg of leftover oxygen, spread around Earth.

20
00:01:08,770 --> 00:01:12,300
~240 atm — Venus: 92 bar
Congratulations, Earth. You beat Venus.

21
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:15,710
0 — Clouds · rain · ice caps
All water. All gone.

22
00:01:16,510 --> 00:01:21,240
550 billion t — Of carbon in living things
Now loose carbon, in a sky of oxygen.

23
00:01:21,240 --> 00:01:26,250
PROBABLY: ONE VERY BIG FIRE.
Speculation. Nobody has modelled this. For obvious reasons.

24
00:01:27,050 --> 00:01:30,350
600 million t — Of hydrogen fused per second
Make that zero.

25
00:01:30,350 --> 00:01:33,940
~70% — Of the sun's mass · gone
Mostly helium is left.

26
00:01:33,940 --> 00:01:36,140
DOES IT EXPLODE?

27
00:01:36,140 --> 00:01:41,730
PROBABLY NOT. — Our rough energy check · uncertain
Sorry. It likely swells and dims. Worse: it loosens its grip.

28
00:01:42,530 --> 00:01:48,000
8 min 19 s — Sun → earth at light speed
Delivery time for bad news. Gravity travels this fast too.

29
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:52,500
29.8 km/s — Earth's speed
Escape speed was 42.1 km/s. Plenty of margin.

30
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:55,170
22–23 km/s — New escape speed
Margin gone.

31
00:01:55,170 --> 00:01:57,770
EARTH LEAVES THE SUN.

32
00:01:58,570 --> 00:02:02,960
~5 AU — From the sun
Near Jupiter's orbit. Jupiter is mostly gone too.

33
00:02:02,960 --> 00:02:07,520
318 — Earth masses · ~¾ hydrogen
The biggest planet, reduced to whatever wasn't hydrogen.

34
00:02:08,320 --> 00:02:12,480
THE STARS GO OUT.
Most of them were mostly hydrogen.

35
00:02:12,480 --> 00:02:15,890
95% — Dark energy + dark matter
Doesn't notice. Never notices.

36
00:02:15,890 --> 00:02:21,190
≈3.6% — Of the universe was hydrogen
Turns out it was the 3.6% doing all the work.

37
00:02:21,990 --> 00:02:25,190
WHICH ELEMENT SHOULD WE DELETE NEXT?

38
00:02:25,190 --> 00:02:29,790
NOT OXYGEN, PLEASE.
We have about 240 atmospheres of it now.

